From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armbian
Date: Tue, 24 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: net: sunxi-gmac: fix EPHY CLK_SEL (bit 18) for H313 internal oscillator

In INT_PHY mode, geth_power_on() used `value |= (3 << 17)` which sets
both bit 17 (LED polarity) and bit 18 (CLK_SEL=1), routing the emac-25m
clock to the EPHY reference input.

On H313 (sun50iw9p1), emac-25m is parented to AHB3 (200 MHz) with no
CCU divider, so CLK_SEL=1 feeds a 200 MHz signal to a port expecting
25 MHz. This corrupts the EPHY PLL and causes MDIO to return 0xffff for
all PHY register reads, which prevents SOFT_RST in EMAC_BASIC_CTL1 from
self-clearing ("All clock inputs must be valid before soft reset" per
H616 datasheet).

Fix: keep CLK_SEL=0 so the EPHY uses its internal 25 MHz RC oscillator.
Bit 17 (LED polarity) is still set.

[MCD125-H313-v1] Tomate MCD-125 board fix.

---
 drivers/net/ethernet/allwinner/sunxi-gmac.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/allwinner/sunxi-gmac.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/allwinner/sunxi-gmac.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/allwinner/sunxi-gmac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/allwinner/sunxi-gmac.c
@@ -831,6 +831,12 @@ static int geth_power_on(struct geth_priv *priv)
     if (priv->phy_ext == INT_PHY) {
         value |= (1 << 15);
         value &= ~(1 << 16);
-        value |= (3 << 17);
+        value |= (1 << 17);
+        /* [MCD125-H313-v1] Keep CLK_SEL (bit 18) = 0: EPHY uses its internal
+         * 25 MHz RC oscillator. emac-25m on H313 runs at 200 MHz (AHB3 parent,
+         * no CCU divider) -- feeding it to EPHY as reference corrupts MDIO.
+         * SOFT_RST in EMAC_BASIC_CTL1 never self-clears without a valid MAC
+         * clock input ("All clock inputs must be valid before soft reset"). */
+        value &= ~(1 << 18);
     } else {
         value &= ~(1 << 15);
